# CODEOWNERS — APP specification repository
#
# This file maps repository paths to the GitHub team(s) whose review is
# required before a pull request touching those paths may be merged.
#
# CODEOWNERS uses LAST-MATCH-WINS semantics. More specific patterns must
# appear LATER in this file to override earlier general ones.
#
# These assignments only REQUEST review by default; the actual blocking
# behaviour is set by the branch ruleset ("Require review from Code
# Owners"), which is activated in Work Package 4.
#
# See /GOVERNANCE.md §2.2 for the approval policy that uses these
# assignments.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: any path not matched below gets Release Approver review.
# This covers top-level governance files (LICENSE, README, CONTRIBUTING,
# GOVERNANCE, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, SECURITY, SECURITY-AUTOMATION, CHANGELOG,
# and anything else at the root).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                  @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workflows and CI tooling — custodians own supply-chain concerns.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/**              @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians
/.github/scripts/**                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians
/.github/actions/**                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians
/.github/dependabot.yml            @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians

# CODEOWNERS itself: both custodians and release-approvers must sign off,
# so no team can unilaterally expand its own review power.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# release-approvers.txt: dual control for the list of authorised sign-off
# identities. Read from the base branch by release-integrity, so a PR cannot
# use its own modified version to pass its check.
/.github/release-approvers.txt     @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# Issue forms and PR template — editors can maintain, release-approvers
# must co-review because template changes affect governance signalling.
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/**         @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/.github/pull_request_template.md  @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Legal, scope, decisions, releases — Release Approver authority.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/legal/**                          @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/csl/**                            @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/decisions/**                      @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/releases/**                       @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# OPERATIONS-REGISTRY: dual control for App / permission grant integrity.
/OPERATIONS-REGISTRY.md            @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Specification drafts.
# Normative drafts default to editors; APP-1 is elevated to custodians +
# release-approvers because of its constitutional significance (listed
# AFTER the general rule so it overrides).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/drafts/spec/APP-[0-5]*            @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/drafts/spec/APP-1*                @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# Informative guides: editors.
/drafts/guides/**                  @agenticprocessprotocol/editors
/guides/**                         @agenticprocessprotocol/editors

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Change-impact manifests — editors prepare, release-approvers verify.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/changes/**                        @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accompanying artefacts (informative, outside the Specification).
# Publication clearance is a Release Approver act; editors do technical
# review.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
/schemas/**                        @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/reference/**                      @agenticprocessprotocol/editors @agenticprocessprotocol/release-approvers
/tools/**                          @agenticprocessprotocol/custodians

# End of CODEOWNERS.
